      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To convert from rectangular to spherical coordinates, note that $\\rho$ represents the radius, which corresponds to the length of the hypotenuse and can be found using\n\\[\\rho = \\sqrt{x^2 + y^2 + z^2}.\\]\nThus, in our case,\n\\[\\rho = \\sqrt{0^2 + (-3\\sqrt3)^2 + 3^2} = \\boxed{\\sqrt{27} = 3\\sqrt{3}}.\\]\nTo find $\\theta$ and $\\phi$, note that\n\\[\\theta = \\tan^{-1} \\left( \\frac{y}{x} \\right) = \\boxed{\\pi},\\]\nand\n\\[\\phi = \\cos^{-1} \\left( \\frac{z}{\\rho} \\right) = \\cos^{-1} \\left( \\frac{3}{3\\sqrt{3}} \\right) = \\cos^{-1} \\left( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\right) = \\boxed{ \\frac{\\pi}{6} }. \\]The answer is: (3\\sqrt{3},\\pi,\\frac{\\pi}{6})",
